<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <title>Pitta n'chiusa</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <h1>Pitta N'chiusa</h1>
        <img
            src="img/pitta_nchiusa.jpeg"
            alt="a tipical suoth italian pie"
            height="500"
            width="500"
        />
        <p>
            The "Pitta N'chiusa is a tipic calabrian pie. It has many shapes but
            the most classic one is composed by tiny rolls that look like roses
            thighty packed together. Is very common to see this fragrant pie on
            the tables on calbrians during the holidays.
        </p>
        <!-- descrizione torta -->
        <!-- ingredienti -->
        <br />
        <h2>Ingredients:</h2>
        <br />
        <h3>What you need</h3>
        <p>
            28 cm low cake tin
        </p>
        <br>
        <h3>For dough</h3>
        <dl>
            <dt>Semolina flour</dt>
            <dd>260gr</dd>
            <dt>00 Flour</dt>
            <dd>50gr</dd>
            <dt>Extra virgin olive oil</dt>
            <dd>70g</dd>
            <dt>granulated sugar</dt>
            <dd>80gr</dd>
            <dt>White Wine</dt>
            <dd>75ml</dd>
            <dt>Water</dt>
            <dd>65ml</dd>
            <dt>Cinnamon</dt>
            <dd>1 teaspoon</dd>
            <dt>Cloves</dt>
            <dd>1/3 teaspoon</dd>
        </dl>
        <h3>For Filling</h3>
        <dl>
            <dt>Nuts</dt>
            <dd>450gr</dd>
            <dt>Raisin</dt>
            <dd>250gr</dd>
            <dt>White wine</dt>
            <dd>60ml</dd>
            <dt>Granulated sugar</dt>
            <dd>100gr</dd>
            <dt>One orange rind</dt>
            <dt>One Mandarin rind</dt> 
            <dt>Cinnamon</dt>
            <dd>1 teaspoon</dd>
            <dt>cloves</dt>
            <dd>1/3</dd>
        </dl>
        <br />
        <ol>
            <li>
                Divide and roll the dough
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Divide the dough into 100g pieces.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Roll each piece using a pasta machine (or rolling pin) into 1mm-thick sheets, 60 cm long and 14 cm wide.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Tip: If the dough cracks or tears, let it rest for 5 minutes under plastic wrap to relax the gluten.    
                    </li>
                </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            Cut the sheets
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Use a fluted wheel to cut each sheet into two 60cm x 7 cm strips.
                    You'll need 9 strips total
                </li>
            </ul>
          </li>  
          <li>
            Prepare the base
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Overlap 3 sheets to form a 28 cm x 28 cm square. Cut out a 28 cm circle and place it on a flat surface lined with par>
Brush the circle with oil, then sprinkle with sugar and spices.

                </li>

            </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                Fill the strips
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Brush the 7 cm-wide strips with oil, then sprinkle with sugar, spices, and a little filling.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Tip: Leave a small margin on the long edge to prevent filling from leaking when folded.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                shape the "roses"
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Fold each strip legthwise to enclose the filling, then roll it
                        into a rose shape
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Roll the end of the strip in the opposite direction to create
                        two connected roses.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                Arrange the roses
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Place 18 roses on the dough circle, pressing them close together to ensure even baking and compactness
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                Seal the edges
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Fold the edges of the dough circle upward to embrace the roses, pleating as needed for a snug fit
                    </li>
                    
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                The with twine
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Use kitchen twine to gently cinch the dough at its midpoint (like a belt). Tie a knot to hold it in place.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Warning: Don't tie too tightly—it should support, not cut into the dough.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                Transfer to the pan
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Place the Pitta 'nchiusa (with parchment) into the cake pan. Brush the surface with oil
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                baking
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Bake in a static oven at 180° C (350°F) for 50 minutes
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Check: The top should be golden, and the base dry and firm. If the top browns too quickly but the base is undercooked
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>

            <li>
                Add honey
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Just before removing from the oven, warm the honey until fluid.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Immediately after baking, drizzle the honey over the hot cake so it seeps into the folds.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
            Cool completely before serving.
        </p>
        <!-- lista passaggi torta -->
    </body >
</html>
